# Nova AI — Implementation Plan

This plan details the technical steps required to implement the structured memory, proactive initiative, and emotional tracking for the Nova AI companion, as outlined in the analysis document.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The biggest architectural change is the introduction of a cron job to handle proactive messaging. Since this runs on the backend server, we need to decide how the frontend will receive these messages.
> 
> My recommendation: For now, have the frontend simply fetch new messages when the user opens the app or the Nova panel. If we want true real-time push (like a notification when the app is open), we would need WebSockets (Socket.io) or Server-Sent Events (SSE). 
> 
> **Are you okay with having the frontend fetch the proactive messages (e.g., polling every minute or fetching on load), or do we already have a WebSocket setup we should use?**

## Proposed Changes

### Database Layer

#### [MODIFY] [schema.prisma](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/prisma/schema.prisma)(file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/prisma/schema.prisma)
Add the `NovaUserMemory` model to store structured facts, trust levels, and emotional trends.

```diff
+// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// AI & NOVA MEMORY SYSTEM
+// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+model NovaUserMemory {
+  id                 String   @id @default(uuid())
+  userId             String   @unique
+  
+  // Fast-lookup structured fields
+  nickname           String?
+  occupation         String?
+  currentMood        String?
+  emotionalTrend     String? // "improving", "declining", "stable"
+  topInterests       String[] // e.g., ["coding", "anime"]
+  lifeGoals          String[]
+  currentStruggles   String[]
+  importantPeople    String[]
+  lastTopicDiscussed String?
+  insideJokes        String[]
+  preferredTone      String?
+  trustLevel         Int      @default(0) // 0-100 scale
+  friendshipStage    String   @default("NEW") // NEW, FAMILIAR, FRIEND, CLOSE, SOULMATE
+  
+  createdAt          DateTime @default(now())
+  updatedAt          DateTime @updatedAt
+  
+  user               User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
+  
+  @@index([userId])
+}
```

Also, update the [User](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-frontend/src/components/layout/HomeSidebar.tsx#27-37) model to include the relation:
```diff
 model User {
   ... existing fields ...
   aiConversations    AIConversation[]
+  novaMemory         NovaUserMemory?
 }
```

### Backend Services

#### [NEW] [memory.service.ts](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/memory.service.ts)(file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/memory.service.ts)
Create a dedicated service to handle the background extraction of structured facts from user messages and the calculation of trust points.
- Implement [extractFactsAndUpdateMemory(userId: string, recentMessages: AIMessage[])](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/memory.service.ts#33-145): Calls groq to extract facts using specialized prompt, upserts `NovaUserMemory`.
- Implement `updateTrustLevel(userId: string, eventType: TrustEvent)`: Adjusts the 0-100 score and calculates `friendshipStage`.

#### [MODIFY] [ai.service.ts](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.service.ts)(file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.service.ts)
Update the core generation logic to use the structured data and support proactivity.
- **Context Builder**: Replace raw text injection with a `buildSmartContext` function that fetches `NovaUserMemory` and filters facts based on keywords in the current user message.
- **Background Extraction**: In [generateResponse](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.service.ts#417-574), after responding, trigger (fire-and-forget) the [memory.service.ts](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/memory.service.ts) extraction process.
- **Proactive Method**: Add [generateProactiveMessage(userId: string, contextType: string)](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.service.ts#607-679) to generate check-ins or context-driven messages.

#### [NEW] [ai.cron.ts](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.cron.ts)(file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.cron.ts)
Create a simple cron job (using `node-cron`) to periodically sweep for users who haven't interacted recently.
- Find users whose last `AIMessage` is older than 24 hours.
- For a sample of these users, call [generateProactiveMessage](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.service.ts#607-679) and save the resulting message to the database (flagged with `isProactive = true`).

#### [MODIFY] [ai.routes.ts](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.routes.ts)(file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.routes.ts) & [ai.controller.ts](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.controller.ts)(file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.controller.ts)
- Expose an endpoint to trigger/fetch proactive messages, or ensure [getChatHistory](file:///D:/pfe/pfe%200.3/soullink-backend/src/modules/ai-companion/ai.controller.ts#30-45) returns them seamlessly so the frontend picks them up.

